From 0c5c27d49fe3acc731cc6ef3b57d0f74a83685d2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TekRantGaming <craigferels896@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 13:25:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] Shared memory: keep GPU written data when the CPU writes
 to the same page

Memory export is not read back, so guest memory lacks what the GPU wrote. A CPU write to such a page used to
reupload the whole page from guest memory, replacing the GPU's data with stale bytes (Trials Evolution expands
particles into a vertex buffer the CPU also writes: stretched triangles and black areas). The page is now saved
before the first CPU write, and only the bytes the CPU changed are uploaded.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
